From: ROG5 build <klimovich008@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tu: enable storageBuffer8BitAccess on a6xx gen4 (A660)

DXVK 3.x hard-requires storageBuffer8BitAccess. Turnip only exposes it on
a7xx (storage_8bit), so DXVK >= 3.0 rejects the Adreno 660 with "Device does
not support required feature 'storageBuffer8BitAccess'".

The 8-bit SSBO path added for a7xx (MR 28254, 39124) is generic ir3/turnip
code: every SSBO descriptor gets an extra R8_UINT buffer descriptor, and 8-bit
loads/stores become scalar typed ldib/stib through it, which is the encoding
of an imageBuffer load/store with an R8_UINT format. a6xx gen4 has has_isam_v
and storage_16bit, which that path asserts, so it needs no other change.

Tested on an Adreno 660 (ASUS ROG Phone 5): 8-bit loads (restrict/readonly
and plain, signed and unsigned), concurrent byte stores to the same 32-bit
words from adjacent lanes and from neighbouring workgroups, byte stores that
must leave the other bytes of a word untouched, immediate offsets, dynamic
offsets and robustBufferAccess2 bounds on a 13-byte range; a racy 32-bit
read-modify-write control in the same test fails, the byte stores do not.
dEQP-VK 8-bit storage groups: see packages/mesa/README.md.

---
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -233,6 +233,11 @@ a6xx_gen4 = GPUProps(
         has_z24uint_s8uint = True,
         tess_use_shared = True,
         storage_16bit = True,
+        # 8-bit SSBO access uses the a7xx path: a dedicated R8_UINT buffer
+        # descriptor and typed ldib/stib, i.e. what an R8_UINT imageBuffer
+        # load/store does, which a6xx already supports. It needs has_isam_v
+        # (below) so that SSBOs need only two descriptors.
+        storage_8bit = True,
         has_tex_filter_cubic = True,
         has_separate_chroma_filter = True,
         has_sample_locations = True,
